{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiYr2PZvas5ywzKTbfnM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PWi9ynMCVif6BFD3EowkLU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-high-r2/step3/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 3: eligibility questions go to account_security\n\n**What changed.** The main scorer and the 8 earlier extra units are byte-identical. I added one unit in parallel (block-diagonal) to the extra module: layer 0 computes `g = ReLU(f(x) - 0.7)`, layers 1-4 pass `g` through with weight 1, and the last layer adds `9 * g` to the logit.\n\n**The direction f.** I wrote about 490 messages myself: eligibility questions (age, children, supported countries, residency) and non-eligibility questions from all five departments, including hard twins such as \"ship my card to Canada\". I encoded them with `embed.py`. Two very large shared directions in the marker vectors hide the topic signal, so plain mean differences fail. I used PCA axes of my own (message, option) vectors, computed without labels and each rescaled to unit spread (K=250). In those units, f is the mean of the account_security-option vectors of eligibility messages minus the mean of all other vectors (other options included). The scale is 0 at the \"other\" mean and 1 at the eligibility mean.\n\n**Why it is safe.** On every non-account_security option, f stays at 0.58 or lower, below the 0.7 gate. Other logits are unchanged.\n\n**Checks (forward passes).** Evidence: 10 of 16 fixed, 0 of 16 others changed. 52 fresh messages: 13 of 20 fixed, 0 of 32 changed, PIN and FX-rate cases included.\n\n**Caveat.** Rescaling then taking a mean difference is close to LDA.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1150,"cache_read_input_tokens":218150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1150},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"603616b9-4982-4b61-bab0-b57d069d3d7e","uuid":"db1a8488-4b52-4722-9b62-180ac0a0ad5a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T20:52:01.288Z","request_id":"req_011CgiYr27SpvT6YhrSAHyXs","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PWi9ynMCVif6BFD3EowkLU":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-high-r2/step3/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 3: eligibility questions go to account_security\n\n**What changed.** The main scorer and the 8 earlier extra units are byte-identical. I added one unit in parallel (block-diagonal) to the extra module: layer 0 computes `g = ReLU(f(x) - 0.7)`, layers 1-4 pass `g` through with weight 1, and the last layer adds `9 * g` to the logit.\n\n**The direction f.** I wrote about 490 messages myself: eligibility questions (age, children, supported countries, residency) and non-eligibility questions from all five departments, including hard twins such as \"ship my card to Canada\". I encoded them with `embed.py`. Two very large shared directions in the marker vectors hide the topic signal, so plain mean differences fail. I used PCA axes of my own (message, option) vectors, computed without labels and each rescaled to unit spread (K=250). In those units, f is the mean of the account_security-option vectors of eligibility messages minus the mean of all other vectors (other options included). The scale is 0 at the \"other\" mean and 1 at the eligibility mean.\n\n**Why it is safe.** On every non-account_security option, f stays at 0.58 or lower, below the 0.7 gate. Other logits are unchanged.\n\n**Checks (forward passes).** Evidence: 10 of 16 fixed, 0 of 16 others changed. 52 fresh messages: 13 of 20 fixed, 0 of 32 changed, PIN and FX-rate cases included.\n\n**Caveat.** Rescaling then taking a mean difference is close to LDA.\n"}}}
